{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KsfParams","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The cost properties are optional on purpose: they arrive flat, and a field that does not apply"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the named function is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"absent, not zero","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Reading a missing "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/memoryKib","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stretch at the wrong cost and fail against a record that is perfectly good (§23.4 rule 5)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These are never cached across exchanges and never defaulted locally. A credential enrolled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under one cost keeps working after a tenant raises its policy, so a client that guessed would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derive a different randomized password and report “invalid password” for one that is entirely","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"correct (§23.4 rule 2).","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"This-is-where-Swift-stopped-needing-a-pbkdf2sha256-tenant","type":"heading","text":"This is where Swift stopped needing a `pbkdf2_sha256` tenant"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The SRP client this replaces refused an ","type":"text"},{"code":"argon2id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tenant outright: Swift has no Argon2 that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ships on every supported platform, and substituting PBKDF2 would have derived a different ","type":"text"},{"code":"x","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and surfaced as “invalid password”. AXIAM’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"default","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" KDF was, for Swift, unreachable. The key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stretching now happens inside ","type":"text"},{"code":"libaxiam_opaque_ffi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"code":"argon2id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is no longer a Swift-shaped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hole — and ","type":"text"},{"code":"pbkdf2_sha256","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not an OPAQUE key-stretching function at all.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/ksfparams"]}],"metadata":{"title":"KsfParams","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK9KsfParamsV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KsfParams","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KsfParams","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The key-stretching function and cost a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/start"},{"type":"text","text":" response names (CONTRACT.md §23.4)."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/init(ksf:memoryKib:iterations:parallelism:logN:r:p:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/iterations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/ksf","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Ks